  "body": "Add a Heidenhain KLAR conversational (`.H`) dialect reader to `camcraft-gcode`.\n\n## Scope\n- Parse native Heidenhain Klartext syntax (`BEGIN PGM ... MM/INCH`, `TOOL CALL`, `L`, `CC`, `C`, `CR`, `CYCL DEF`, `CYCL CALL`, `M99`, `END PGM`) from public HEIDENHAIN TNC programming manuals (`assets/posts/heidenhain.cps` lines 1-4 note KLAR as separate from DIN/ISO).\n- Emit `cl::Toolpath` moves with 1-based block numbers and expand supported drilling cycles (`CYCL DEF 200`/`205`/`206`/`207`).\n- Refuse unsupported conversational cycles, polar syntax, or unknown tokens by name with the block number.\n\nDepends on #2217.\n\nDone means: Tests parse KLAR `.H` programs with `L` moves, `CC`/`C`/`CR` arcs, and drilling cycles into `cl::Toolpath` sections and refuse unsupported cycles by name and block number.\n\nPart of #2213\n",
